== About Me

I am an undergraduate physics student at
The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen.

My research interests focus on experimental particle physics,
particularly dark matter direct detection, neutrino physics,
and detector calibration.

I am currently involved in the XENONnT experiment,
working on detector response characterization and
signal reconstruction efficiency.

== Research Interests

- Dark Matter Direct Detection
- Neutrino Physics
- Detector Calibration and Reconstruction
- Experimental Data Analysis

== Selected Research

=== XENONnT Detector Response

Calibration and characterization of the XENONnT detector
response during Science Run 2, including the determination
of light and charge gains and energy resolution.

=== Solar pp Neutrino ACE

Investigation of signal reconstruction and analysis-cut
efficiencies using detector simulation and waveform
injection techniques.

